# Merged over the image's config.yaml by CrowdSec's own `.local` overlay, so the
# container still populates and owns config.yaml itself. Hand-maintained: unlike
# acquis.d/ beside it, nothing renders this file.
#
# Pinning the hub branch is what keeps a start independent of the CrowdSec hub.
# Left unset, every `cscli` hub command resolves the branch by fetching
# version.crowdsec.net first, and the entrypoint runs two *unconditional*
# `cscli parsers install` calls (docker-logs, cri-logs) on every start, neither
# guarded by `|| true`. Under the entrypoint's `set -e`, a failed install and
# its equally unguarded retry exit the entrypoint, so an unreachable hub
# crash-loops the container even when every item is already installed and
# current. With the branch pinned, cscli never makes that call and the installs
# are a local no-op.
#
# The value must stay whatever `cscli hub branch` resolves to for the pinned
# image version -- re-check it with that command when the digest is bumped.
cscli:
  hub_branch: master
